 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Crisis at the Restaurant", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Still Waiting \u2026", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe emotions and feelings in present and past situations in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Willingness, Refusal, Promises and Threats", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">Will</span> or <span class=\"italic\">Won't</span> to express willingness, refusal, promise and threat in situations in the present or in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " There are different ways to use <span class=\"italic\">will</span> or <span class=\"italic\">won't</span>. In the following uses, we don't necessarily talk about a future action or an event that will take place at a point in time in the future. Instead, <span class=\"italic\">will</span> or <span class=\"italic\">won't</span> are used to express willingness, refusal, promise or threat related to an action which could be in the present or in the future. <br><br> Look at the following examples: <br> <br><span class=\"bullet\">Willingness:</span> <br><span class=\"italic\">Will you clean the restaurant kitchen with me, please?</span> <br> <br><span class=\"bullet\">Refusal:</span> <br><span class=\"italic\">I will not tolerate this behavior in the kitchen any longer.</span> <br><span class=\"italic\">The computer won't start.</span> <br> <br><span class=\"bullet\">Promise:</span> <br><span class=\"italic\">I'll do everything I can to satisfy our customers.</span> <br> <br><span class=\"bullet\">Threat:</span> <br><span class=\"italic\">If you refuse to help me, I'll have to take extreme measures.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Well if you won't tell me then put me through to someone who will.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Will you open the bags of ice and put them in the large sink? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Can you promise you'll be here to get ice if we need it?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Purpose Clauses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use purpose clauses to express the reasons for an action, or the intended motive of a specific situation. <br>You use words like <span class=\"italic\">to, in order to, so as to </span>to introduce a purpose clause.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " Purpose clauses are subordinate to the main clause. The order of the clauses can be interchangeable, as long as the relationship between the two remains clear. <br>Example: <br><span class=\"italic\">I have come up with a new plan <span class=\"strong\">in order to</span> stay focused. <br><span class=\"strong\">In order to</span> stay focused, I have come up with a new plan.</span> <br> <br>You use <span class=\"italic\">to</span> with an infinitive as a way to express purpose. We refer to this structure as an Infinitive of purpose. <br>Example: <span class=\"italic\">I called <span class=\"strong\">to</span> find out if the order had been shipped.</span> <br> <br>You use <span class=\"italic\">in order to</span> or <span class=\"italic\">so as to</span> to emphasize an intention or a necessity. <br>Example:  <br><span class=\"italic\">I would like to call for a meeting <span class=\"strong\">in order to / so as to</span> address the current issues in the restaurant. <br> <br>You use <span class=\"italic\">in order that</span> or <span class=\"italic\">so that</span> when the second clause starts with a pronoun or a noun. <br>Example: <br><span class=\"italic\">You need to give me an answer, <span class=\"strong\">so that / in order that</span> I can address the problem quickly.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You need to give me an answer in order that I know whether to cancel tonight's reservations or not! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "So as not to go completely ballistic, I have come up with a shortened dinner service. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I am here in order to help you.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to function ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to work or operate in a proper or particular way ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I can't function without my fridge.   ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about customer relations.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ambiguity ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "uncertainty or inexactness of meaning in language ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: No more ambiguity!  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to put someone through", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to connect someone by telephone to another person or place ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Well if you won't tell me then put me through to someone who will.   ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to go ballistic ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to become enraged ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: So as not to go completely ballistic, I have come up with a shortened dinner service and a limited menu for tonight. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to close up shop ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cease business operation ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Why not close up shop for 24 hours?   ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "admirable ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "deserving respect and approval ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Your loyalty and perseverance  are admirable.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sanity ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the ability to think and behave in a normal and rational manner ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My sanity hinges on Jim bringing those darn hoses!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "of utmost importance", "type": "name"}, {"content": "of greatest concern", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Your being consistant is of utmost importance.   ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob05aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to hinge on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to depend upon ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My sanity hinges on Jim bringing those darn hoses!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob05aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online and watch a video on youtube to find out how to deal with an angry customer.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down key ideas on each point.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your notes to a friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss how effective you think the advice is.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I listen to advice on dealing with an angry customer.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write down key ideas.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present my notes to a friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss what I think about the advice.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}